    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d610">

                <pb facs="0681" n="671" sameAs="frus:frus1943v01/pg671"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Moscow/92: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Delegation to
                        the Acting Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-10-30T09:00:00+03:00">October 30, 1943—9
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 10:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Delam 43. From McDermott. Penultimate paragraph only of Delam No. 35<anchor
                        n="32" xml:id="d610-f1"/> is now canceled and the following arrangement
                    substituted. Arrangements agreed upon by American, British and USSR delegations
                    are that Moscow stories of the close and results of conference shall be released
                    simultaneously in the three countries <pb facs="0682" n="672" xml:id="pg672"/>
                    at midnight Monday, Moscow time, 5 p.m., Eastern War Time, November 1st. Censor
                    will permit correspondents to begin filing at 4 p.m. Moscow time, November 1st.
                    Should the Germans tap the news transmissions, any publishable pickups of German
                    broadcasts on the subject are not to be published or rebroadcast in the United
                    States, Great Britain or Russia until after publication of the Moscow stories.
                    [McDermott.]</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
